 ## Darwin v4.5.3 cargo-internal-rewire transition
 
 The Darwin arm64 contract recorded a reviewed internal `Cargo.lock` rewire at v4.5.3 from the native artifact 12093899220 of [workflow_dispatch run 39015514836](https://github.com/Takazudo/zudo-front-builder/actions/runs/39015514836) (job 117346719895) at source `792c812325310df73540cc20aa590bb8de049d96`: `Cargo.lock` moved from `13956cf2b75baea8b68442c750174714b9591d6ab7ba9f923a800c5653e1ac37` to `230f0acb80e141c66dc5cfe50d028a840103ea8fcce5ff88250b7b0668e1b138` by adding 1 internal record(s) (`zfb-js-host@0.0.0`) and rewiring 1 internal record(s) (`zfb-render@0.0.0` removes `sha1`, `sha2`, adds `zfb-js-host`); every other `[[package]]` record and the header are byte-identical, as declared in `prototypes/direct-v8/evidence/cargo-rewire-main-e1ef4f5b/declaration.json` (SHA-256 `204a8fa17f043503e652a0a8811d07e3143966cfb4ce490ac4429ed0104a369b`) and proved against `Cargo.lock` at commit `e1ef4f5b59a2bba260eac29ee8edfdfbcd928335` (SHA-256 `13956cf2b75baea8b68442c750174714b9591d6ab7ba9f923a800c5653e1ac37`). The `zfb` producer closure for `aarch64-apple-darwin` keeps 481 rows unchanged, adds 1 and changes 0 internal row(s) with no external package, version, source or feature drift (receipts `db24ecb9aba788f0c8c5483a5f235e991ff9905c5685ef837c9bbe79cf1ac77d` and `d1bb5bd0e0ecdb978b069761891e9961b27f2ceffe30dac49fb01be1aabbfb1e`). The package version, fixtures, runners, `pnpm-lock.yaml` and its dependency fingerprint, toolchain and normalizer are unchanged, and every raw and `gzipNormalized` total is unchanged; only `toolchain.cargoLockSha256` moved. These totals alone do not prove byte-identical product code. The artifact's own `check-budget.mjs` run against the previous pin is preserved as evidence (exit code 1). No actual gzip total moved. Linux x64 moves in the same paired change (`--stage`, then `--apply`).
+
+## v4.5.3 cargo-producer-lock transition
+
+The Linux contract recorded a reviewed non-additive `Cargo.lock` transition at v4.5.3 from [workflow run 39302891207](https://github.com/Takazudo/zudo-front-builder/actions/runs/39302891207) (job 118232731946) at PR merge source `e397161c609e780a79ec4273c907168355518aab` (probe head `0355ad78a4f8d2c240844d2b48da7c2769f6de25`): `Cargo.lock` moved from `230f0acb80e141c66dc5cfe50d028a840103ea8fcce5ff88250b7b0668e1b138` to `563194257102ac98a57ba6561fc0084c35518aaf83e21f68106d07e0c604f5bd` under reviewed non-additive transition `rustls-security-4314` (manifest SHA-256 `fe689aca3a29b012ca7fb96a3aad3dc9fc507f117a18be501e379dae2b3f04ff`): 1 new identities, 0 changed records and 1 removed identities, proved against `21d6807e442bbed61e578c165a91d64c4a7dc141:Cargo.lock`. The producer version, fixtures, runners, `pnpm-lock.yaml` and its dependency fingerprint, toolchain and normalizer are unchanged, and every raw and `gzipNormalized` total is unchanged; only `toolchain.cargoLockSha256` moved. These totals alone do not prove byte-identical product code. Actual gzip moved on 11 rows by -3 to +4 bytes (workspace show-for +3, model -2, blog-theme, json-api and scalar-signal -3; packed json-api +4, multi-island +3, blog-theme +2, model +1, event-only and scalar-signal -1); that is transfer-size evidence in the sidecar, not a ceiling. The retained `island-size-linux-x64` artifact contains all eight fixtures in both modes with two identical full-dist inventories per case. `decision-linux-x64.json` records the `raw` and `gzipNormalized` totals as exact ceilings with zero allowance; earlier ceilings remain in git history. The Darwin arm64 contract is unchanged; it is re-pinned separately from a native `island-size-darwin.yml` artifact by `rebaseline-island-size-darwin.mjs`.
